From: M2 Gate Closure Audit <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:48:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs(H3.4): record boundary-loss curve (n=21..200)

H3.4 (empirical): measured achieved density vs. the H3.2 cell density
(0.725241) across the full n=21..200 sweep using H3.3's truncate_to_n.
Not falsified -- loss at n=50 is 35.0%, far above the 3% floor that would
indicate truncation is already near-optimal.

Every measured loss is larger than the milestone doc's own worked-example
numbers at the same n (e.g. 35.0% vs. its 18% at n=50; 18.3% vs. its 6% at
n=200), recorded as expected given H3.3's known limitation (no SA
swap-move refinement yet) rather than treated as a surprise or smoothed
over. Lumpiness confirmed: loss is not monotone in n (n=172 loses less
than n=150 or n=200), matching the milestone's own observation.

Sum of configuration_score terms across n=21..200 alone (lattice
truncation only, no M2 post-processes, n=1..20 not yet covered): 83.537.

No code changes; LAB_NOTEBOOK.md only.
